# Hostile self-audit — bounded-face train endpoint simplicity

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Audited source:** `target_c_bounded_face_endpoint_simplicity_2026-09-12.md`  
**Disposition:** PASS at the stated proof-only scope; theorem-state authority unchanged.  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.

The canonical train midpoint geometry supplies simple arcs with at most one crossing.
Disjoint paths are closed through the two empty bounded-face interiors; crossing paths
are reduced to an innermost lens or a prefix cycle. The resulting Jordan interior lies
in the source hull, so extreme active diameter endpoints cannot be inside it.

Summed KKT equilibrium over the inside core shore has no diameter term and only the
two selected train resultants. Positive contact weights make each resultant nonzero;
two nonparallel projective directions cannot cancel. The parallel case is exactly the
audited same-direction pair-cut theorem and contradicts the canonical mixed-rank
identity. A singleton train is handled by a sufficiently short transverse midpoint
representative; if a normalization omits that representative, the conclusion is read
only for represented non-singleton trains.

The audit does not extend to outer-face endpoints, unglobalized local segments, or the
aggregate detour/payment problem. Contact-isolated source points remain outside the
core matrix.

**Final audit verdict:** PASS as a proof-only bounded-face endpoint lemma.
